53,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
54,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A could create arrears and social distance. Option B is a temporary fix. Option C removes the ""ownership"" conflict entirely.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option A sounds fair for the daily riders! But Option C sounds so friendly, like we're all sharing together!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C solves the ""my spot"" problem and the morning congestion, though the hardware might be a bit clunky.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A generates income for our empty ledger, but Option B is the cheapest to implement. Option C is a gamble.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is an administrative nightmare. Option B is simple but repetitive. Option C requires maintenance but less paperwork.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the income from Option A isn't worth the risk of neighbors stopping coming to meetings due to payment disputes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, do you think the double-tier racks in Option C would be too hard for some people to use?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, they take a bit of effort, but it's better than waking up to a wet saddle or a blocked exit.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, you're being overly cautious. A small fee is a standard way to handle limited resources in a building.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, you're ignoring the labor. I'd rather have a lottery once a year than a billing cycle every month.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I cannot support Option A. The social cost is too high. I prefer Option C to break the cycle of stagnant ownership.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I love the idea of sharing! Let's go with Option C so everyone can just park and go!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is the most practical for the actual flow of bikes. It eliminates the ""shoving match"" and the fixed-spot resentment.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If we can't agree on payment, Option B is the most neutral, though it doesn't solve the physical issues Ryuji mentioned.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the safest for the association's workload. However, Option C is acceptable if the maintenance is minimal.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Option C. It's the only way to truly reset the atmosphere in the parking area.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I vote for Option C! Let's make it a happy, shared space for everyone!","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for Option C. It's the only choice that addresses the physical congestion and the rain exposure issues.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Since the majority seems to lean toward the racks, I'll concede. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I'll go with the consensus to avoid further conflict. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
